  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 102.33 Proof by a preponderance of the evidence",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 102.33 “Proof by a preponderance of the evidence” means a demonstration by admissible evidence that a fact or legal conclusion is more probable than not to be true.\n\nSource. #10217, eff 10-30-12, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cul-h100.html"
